Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects technical zero events in single-cell RNA-seq data after
    ALRA-style library-size normalization and log transformation. The production
    detector applies native-ALRA-style randomized low-rank reconstruction and the
    gene-wise empirical 0.1 percent quantile zero gate globally within each major
    cell class, while SuperCell memberships and retained hierarchy remain reserved
    for biologically local recovery. Historical membership-local empirical-Bayes
    and ALRA-quantile detectors remain available for explicit comparison. Recovery
    can combine hierarchy proximity with the original biological embedding so
    nearer positive donors contribute more strongly to query-specific expression
    baselines and local coexpression residual models. Predictive uncertainty is
    retained and observed non-dropout values are never overwritten on the
    normalized working scale.
